Package: ducknetview
Version: _version_
Architecture: amd64
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Vladislav Ananev <nexus.riot@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/nexusriot/ducknetview
Installed-Size: _installed_size_
Description: terminal network monitoring TUI
 ducknetview watches a host's network from the terminal: interfaces and their
 throughput, listening sockets, per-process and per-connection traffic, active
 and recently closed connections, a log of what changed, and the routing
 configuration.
 .
 On Linux, per-connection throughput, round-trip time and retransmit counts are
 read from the kernel's sock_diag netlink interface - the same source ss(8)
 uses - so no elevated privileges are required. Listening sockets can be
 recorded as a baseline and checked from cron, and the whole state can be
 exported as JSON or Prometheus metrics.
